  "details": "Feature Request\n\nPlease add a new instance type between Friends and Friends+ that allows only the instance owner’s direct friends and those friends’ direct friends to join, without allowing the join permission to expand any further.\n\nAs a proposal, a clear name for this new option could be \"Friends of Friends\" or \"Friends+ Limited\".\n\nCurrent Problem\n\nAt the moment, \"Friends\" instances are often too restrictive because only the instance owner’s direct friends can join. On the other hand, \"Friends+\" instances can become too open because access can effectively expand through friends of friends, then their friends, and so on. In practice, a Friends+ instance can grow far beyond the original social circle the instance owner intended.\n\nThis creates a gap between two common use cases:\n\n- I want a social instance that is not fully private.\n\n- I want my friends to be able to bring their own friends.\n\n- But I do not want the instance to keep expanding through multiple layers of social connections.\n\nProposed Behavior\n\nAdd a new instance type with these access rules:\n\n1. The instance owner can join.\n\n2. The instance owner’s direct friends can join.\n\n3. The direct friends of those friends can also join.\n\n4. Users beyond that second-degree connection cannot join unless they are directly invited by the instance owner or otherwise allowed by a separate manual invite rule.\n\nIn other words:\n\n- Friends: owner’s friends only.\n\n- Friends+: broader friend-chain access.\n\n- New type: owner’s friends + friends of those friends only, with no third-degree or further expansion.\n\nWhy This Would Help\n\nThis would give instance owners more precise control over the size and social scope of their instances. It would be useful for semi-private hangouts, small events, community meetups, game sessions, and social groups where some openness is desired but uncontrolled growth is not.\n\nIt would also reduce the need for awkward manual moderation, repeated kicks, or switching to a much more restrictive instance type after the instance has already become too large or too far removed from the original group.\n\nThis request is not asking to change the current Friends+ behavior. Friends+ should remain available for users who want a more open social instance. The request is simply to add a middle option for users who want controlled friend-of-friend access without unlimited chain expansion.",
